This project includes unmodified source contracts from xiaok-cli
(https://github.com/kaisersong/xiaok-cli), licensed under Apache-2.0:
  desktop/electron/room-workspace-protocol.ts
  desktop/shared/room-external-discussion.ts
Exact revision and SHA-256 digests are recorded in sources.lock.json.
The full Apache-2.0 license is included in LICENSE.

The selected, unmodified xiaok runtime source closure in vendor/xiaok-runtime
is also Apache-2.0. Its full originating revision, upstream file paths and
individual SHA-256 digests are recorded in sources.lock.json under runtime.
KTeam-specific integration lives outside that snapshot.

The xiaok A2UI renderer sources under desktop/xiaok are also unmodified
Apache-2.0 sources. Their original paths and hashes are in sources.lock.json.
Checked build-time runtime adaptations are recorded separately from original bytes.

KSwarm and intent-broker are reused through semantic service adapters.
Their local source packages are development-only integration dependencies.

AIMP 3.1 and the product design baseline were supplied by the project owner.
Their original text, test-vector provenance and review limitations are retained.

KTeam direct local Agent integration reuses source-pinned KSwarm runtime-capabilities.js, kimi-cli-harness.js and pi-cli-harness.js (Apache-2.0), and the existing Intent Broker participant registration protocol. Native CLI programs remain separately installed and retain their own licenses and configuration.

The original xiaok builtin Skills shipped in desktop/skills (except KTeam's own collaboration Skill) are unchanged Apache-2.0 source assets; their originating paths and digests are recorded in sources.lock.json.

KTeam bundles kai-report-creator and kai-slide-creator from kai-xiaok-plugins
(https://github.com/kaisersong/kai-xiaok-plugins), Apache-2.0. The pinned revision
and host adaptations are recorded in sources.lock.json under creatorPlugins.
Their Python interpreter and dependency licenses ship inside build/plugins.
